<title>UK: Aluminium stocks fell in October - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium stocks fell in October - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total stocks of all forms of aluminium at Western world smelters excluding finished end-products, fell to 3.161 million tonnes at the end of October 1996, compared with 3.257 million in September and 3.603 million in October 1995, provisional International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) figures show.</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks fell to 1.686 million tonnes versus 1.747 million and 1.983 million, respectively.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of the total aluminium stocks was as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			    Oct'96   Sep'96    Oct'95</p>
<p>    Africa		    70	 67	  69</p>
<p>    North America	1,495    1,548     1,655</p>
<p>    Latin America	  163	182	 205</p>
<p>    Asia		     165	159	 162</p>
<p>    Europe		 1,119    1,173     1,350</p>
<p>    Oceania		  149	128	 162</p>
<p>Unwrought metal stocks were distributed as follows, in thousands of tonnes.</p>
<p>			   Oct'96    Sep'96    Oct'95</p>
<p>    Africa		   24	  22	  28</p>
<p>    North America	 679	 721	 772</p>
<p>    Latin America	 119	 133	 159</p>
<p>    Asia		    139	 132	 135</p>
<p>    Europe		  611	 647	 777</p>
<p>    Oceania		 114	  92	 112</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
